1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,710
You wake up at seven in the morning,

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:03,330
and floating in front of your

3
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:05,250
chest is a translucent menu.

4
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:06,930
Save point created.

5
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:09,290
At first, you think you're still dreaming.

6
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:10,990
You swipe your hand through it,

7
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:14,050
but your fingers buzz with a mild electric hum.

8
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:16,670
Then small text appears beneath it:

9
00:00:17,130 --> 00:00:19,150
Tap your wrists together twice to reload.

10
00:00:19,890 --> 00:00:20,650
You look out the window.

11
00:00:21,310 --> 00:00:22,010
The streets are moving,

12
00:00:22,350 --> 00:00:22,950
buses are running,

13
00:00:23,410 --> 00:00:24,930
the world is completely normal.

14
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:26,090
Except for you.

15
00:00:26,590 --> 00:00:27,870
For the next seven days,

16
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:29,970
you have one active save point.

17
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:31,330
No matter what happens,

18
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:33,830
no matter what embarrassing mistake you make,

19
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:35,370
what bad news you hear,

20
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:36,790
or what disaster strikes,

21
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:38,470
two taps of your wrists,

22
00:00:38,470 --> 00:00:41,210
and you're back in bed at seven o'clock this morning

23
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:43,370
with full memory of everything that happened.

24
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:46,370
At first, it feels like godhood.

25
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:47,830
By day seven,

26
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:50,590
it becomes the most terrifying prison ever created.

27
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:53,150
At first, it's just pure,

28
00:00:53,150 --> 00:00:54,590
unrestrained freedom.

29
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:55,930
Because your whole life,

30
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,870
fear has been your silent manager.

31
00:00:57,870 --> 00:00:59,210
Fear of looking stupid.

32
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:00,270
Fear of rejection.

33
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:01,890
Fear of losing money.

34
00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:03,250
At the coffee shop,

35
00:01:03,390 --> 00:01:05,190
the person you've had a crush on for six

36
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:06,530
months is standing by the counter.

37
00:01:07,090 --> 00:01:08,490
Normally, your brain calculates

38
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:10,470
forty-seven reasons to stay silent.

39
00:01:11,030 --> 00:01:11,310
Today?

40
00:01:11,630 --> 00:01:12,650
You walk right up,

41
00:01:12,790 --> 00:01:13,570
look them in the eye,

42
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:14,890
and say the boldest,

43
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:17,230
most direct compliment you've ever thought of.

44
00:01:17,770 --> 00:01:18,310
They blush.

45
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:18,930
They smile.

46
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:20,730
They hand you their number on a napkin.

47
00:01:21,290 --> 00:01:22,290
You walk outside,

48
00:01:22,390 --> 00:01:23,670
grinning from ear to ear.

49
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:25,690
Then you see your boss pulling

50
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:26,930
into the office parking lot.

51
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:29,770
You walk right up to him and tell him exactly what everyone

52
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:31,610
in the department thinks of his Saturday emails.

53
00:01:32,110 --> 00:01:33,010
His face turns purple.

54
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:34,570
He screams that you're fired.

55
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:35,630
You smile.

56
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:37,510
You tap your wrists together twice.

57
00:01:38,210 --> 00:01:38,650
Back in bed.

58
00:01:39,110 --> 00:01:40,330
Seven o'clock.

59
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:41,490
The boss has no idea.

60
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:43,070
The argument never happened.

61
00:01:43,590 --> 00:01:44,530
The world was reset,

62
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:46,830
but the experience stayed in your head.

63
00:01:47,510 --> 00:01:49,670
Lesson one: living without fear

64
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:50,810
feels like a superpower.

65
00:01:51,690 --> 00:01:52,670
By day two,

66
00:01:53,090 --> 00:01:54,050
the games get bigger.

67
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:55,650
You watch the opening bell.

68
00:01:56,310 --> 00:01:57,570
You note which stock spikes

69
00:01:57,570 --> 00:01:58,910
three hundred percent by noon.

70
00:01:59,450 --> 00:02:00,130
Then you reload.

71
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:01,730
At seven in the morning,

72
00:02:01,910 --> 00:02:04,710
you put your entire savings into that exact trade.

73
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:06,970
By lunch, you're wealthy.

74
00:02:07,810 --> 00:02:08,790
By day three,

75
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:11,730
you've tried thirty-two different ways to handle your

76
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:14,750
morning meeting until you deliver a presentation so

77
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:17,670
flawless your manager gives you a standing ovation.

78
00:02:18,230 --> 00:02:19,550
You feel invincible.

79
00:02:20,030 --> 00:02:22,110
Until five o'clock on day three.

80
00:02:22,110 --> 00:02:23,630
You're sitting on your couch,

81
00:02:23,630 --> 00:02:25,170
looking at your bank account,

82
00:02:25,370 --> 00:02:27,450
and something cold creeps into your stomach.

83
00:02:28,130 --> 00:02:29,090
You want to order dinner,

84
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:31,130
but suddenly, you hesitate.

85
00:02:31,830 --> 00:02:33,310
What if the pizza place is slow tonight?

86
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:35,350
What if the sushi place is better?

87
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:37,390
Normally, you'd just pick one,

88
00:02:37,390 --> 00:02:38,550
eat, and move on.

89
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:39,530
Now?

90
00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:40,670
You order pizza,

91
00:02:41,170 --> 00:02:41,830
eat two slices,

92
00:02:42,330 --> 00:02:43,030
tap your wrists,

93
00:02:43,390 --> 00:02:44,670
reload, and order sushi.

94
00:02:45,150 --> 00:02:47,230
Then you reload again because you wonder if

95
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:49,210
the Thai curry was the optimal choice.

96
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,590
Psychologists have a name for this:

97
00:02:52,090 --> 00:02:53,350
Maximization Paralysis.

98
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:55,890
When mistakes are impossible to undo,

99
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:58,710
humans accept good-enough outcomes.

100
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:01,990
When every choice can theoretically be perfected,

101
00:03:02,010 --> 00:03:03,970
satisfaction drops to zero.

102
00:03:04,370 --> 00:03:06,670
Because now, every minor imperfection

103
00:03:06,670 --> 00:03:08,530
is your fault for not resetting.

104
00:03:08,990 --> 00:03:09,970
On day four,

105
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:12,110
reality stops being a game.

106
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:13,070
At two fifteen,

107
00:03:13,070 --> 00:03:14,670
you're walking across Fifth Street.

108
00:03:15,170 --> 00:03:17,890
A delivery van runs a red light and clips a cyclist.

109
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:19,530
You scream, rush over,

110
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:20,530
and see blood on the pavement.

111
00:03:21,070 --> 00:03:21,910
Instinct kicks in.

112
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:23,090
You tap your wrists.

113
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:24,570
You wake up.

114
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:26,850
You have seven hours to prevent it.

115
00:03:27,430 --> 00:03:28,070
At two ten,

116
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:29,770
you stand at that exact intersection.

117
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:31,530
When the cyclist arrives,

118
00:03:31,790 --> 00:03:33,170
you step in front of him and ask for

119
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:35,090
directions to delay him by thirty seconds.

120
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:37,150
He stops, points down the street,

121
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:37,610
annoyed.

122
00:03:38,170 --> 00:03:40,770
The delivery van speeds past through the intersection.

123
00:03:41,430 --> 00:03:41,930
No crash.

124
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:43,890
You breathe a sigh of relief.

125
00:03:44,630 --> 00:03:45,470
You saved him.

126
00:03:46,030 --> 00:03:47,050
Until you turn the corner.

127
00:03:47,650 --> 00:03:49,250
Because you delayed the cyclist,

128
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:51,670
the delivery van entered the next intersection

129
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:53,590
two seconds earlier than before.

130
00:03:53,950 --> 00:03:56,570
Where it slammed directly into a crowded city bus.

131
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:58,050
Four people are injured.

132
00:03:58,670 --> 00:03:59,110
You reload.

133
00:04:00,170 --> 00:04:01,070
You wake up at seven.

134
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:02,110
Heart pounding.

135
00:04:02,830 --> 00:04:03,030
Sweating.

136
00:04:03,690 --> 00:04:04,350
You try again.

137
00:04:04,810 --> 00:04:06,190
You pull the fire alarm in the coffee

138
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:07,650
shop to delay the van driver.

139
00:04:08,210 --> 00:04:09,830
That causes a traffic jam that blocks

140
00:04:09,830 --> 00:04:11,550
an ambulance three miles away.

141
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:13,190
No matter what you tweak,

142
00:04:13,730 --> 00:04:15,490
chaotic systems refuse to be tamed.

143
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:17,090
In complex systems,

144
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,370
eliminating one point of friction always

145
00:04:19,370 --> 00:04:21,250
displaces energy somewhere else.

146
00:04:21,770 --> 00:04:22,550
By day five,

147
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:23,330
you haven't slept.

148
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:26,190
You've lived through Tuesday nineteen times.

149
00:04:26,790 --> 00:04:28,170
You realize the horrible truth:

150
00:04:28,670 --> 00:04:29,630
you aren't playing god.

151
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:32,990
You're just a frantic janitor trying to mop the ocean.

152
00:04:33,650 --> 00:04:35,090
On day six,

153
00:04:35,090 --> 00:04:37,550
you decide not to touch the outside world.

154
00:04:38,050 --> 00:04:38,830
You stay inside.

155
00:04:39,330 --> 00:04:40,510
You spend the whole day with

156
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:41,850
the people who matter most:

157
00:04:42,350 --> 00:04:43,230
your closest friend,

158
00:04:43,590 --> 00:04:45,010
your partner, your family.

159
00:04:45,570 --> 00:04:46,810
You have the most heartfelt,

160
00:04:47,050 --> 00:04:49,090
honest conversation of your life.

161
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:50,530
Your friend cries.

162
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:53,430
They tell you things they've never shared with anyone.

163
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:54,570
You hug.

164
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:56,830
It is the deepest human connection

165
00:04:56,830 --> 00:04:58,050
you've ever experienced.

166
00:04:58,890 --> 00:05:00,790
Then, right before you go to bed,

167
00:05:00,790 --> 00:05:02,730
your friend accidentally knocks over

168
00:05:02,730 --> 00:05:04,650
your grandfather's vintage coffee mug.

169
00:05:04,890 --> 00:05:06,530
It shatters across the tiles.

170
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:08,050
They look horrified,

171
00:05:08,490 --> 00:05:09,430
apologizing repeatedly.

172
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:11,270
You look at the shards.

173
00:05:11,590 --> 00:05:12,410
You look at your wrists.

174
00:05:12,990 --> 00:05:13,770
It's so easy.

175
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:15,010
Just two taps.

176
00:05:15,410 --> 00:05:16,870
The mug will be back on the shelf.

177
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:18,410
You tap your wrists.

178
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:20,910
The mug is sitting safely on the counter.

179
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:22,450
Two hours later,

180
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:23,490
your friend comes over.

181
00:05:23,910 --> 00:05:24,890
You smile at them,

182
00:05:24,890 --> 00:05:26,110
feeling that warm,

183
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:27,810
deep bond from yesterday.

184
00:05:28,350 --> 00:05:30,210
You bring up what they told you in tears.

185
00:05:30,890 --> 00:05:32,650
They look at you with total confusion.

186
00:05:33,550 --> 00:05:34,550
What are you talking about?

187
00:05:34,970 --> 00:05:36,190
I never said that.

188
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:38,230
A pit opens in your stomach.

189
00:05:38,830 --> 00:05:39,890
They didn't say that.

190
00:05:40,130 --> 00:05:41,170
Not in this reality.

191
00:05:41,870 --> 00:05:43,390
The breakthrough, the vulnerability,

192
00:05:43,770 --> 00:05:46,030
the tears, the sacred moment,

193
00:05:46,330 --> 00:05:48,230
it only happened in your private,

194
00:05:48,230 --> 00:05:49,170
erased memory.

195
00:05:49,730 --> 00:05:51,550
To them, it never existed.

196
00:05:52,330 --> 00:05:53,830
In erasing the broken mug,

197
00:05:54,170 --> 00:05:56,570
you erased the memory that bonded you together.

198
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:58,930
You are now completely alone with

199
00:05:58,930 --> 00:06:00,870
memories no one else will ever share.

200
00:06:01,630 --> 00:06:02,950
Day seven arrives.

201
00:06:03,390 --> 00:06:04,870
The prompt is counting down.

202
00:06:05,250 --> 00:06:06,810
You have five minutes to decide:

203
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:09,630
do you reload one last time to your safety net,

204
00:06:10,150 --> 00:06:11,890
or do you let the clock strike midnight

205
00:06:11,890 --> 00:06:13,230
and surrender to the unknown?

206
00:06:14,130 --> 00:06:15,110
You look at your hands.

207
00:06:15,650 --> 00:06:16,650
For seven days,

208
00:06:16,650 --> 00:06:19,130
you tried to craft an existence without pain,

209
00:06:19,490 --> 00:06:21,630
without embarrassment, without heartbreak.

210
00:06:22,050 --> 00:06:22,870
And what did you get?

211
00:06:23,490 --> 00:06:24,090
Paralysis.

212
00:06:24,510 --> 00:06:24,990
Isolation.

213
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:26,910
A life where nothing matters

214
00:06:26,910 --> 00:06:28,490
because nothing carries weight.

215
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:31,310
Psychologist Carl Jung wrote that to be

216
00:06:31,310 --> 00:06:34,370
alive is to bear the tension of opposites.

217
00:06:34,530 --> 00:06:37,070
Courage only exists because danger is real.

218
00:06:37,810 --> 00:06:39,950
Love only matters because loss is possible.

219
00:06:40,670 --> 00:06:43,150
Joy only tastes sweet because bad days exist.

220
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:44,610
The menu flashes:

221
00:06:45,290 --> 00:06:46,290
Ten seconds remaining.

222
00:06:46,950 --> 00:06:47,470
Reload?

223
00:06:47,470 --> 00:06:49,850
Magi puts his hands by his side.

224
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:52,390
He lets his wrists stay apart.

225
00:06:53,190 --> 00:06:54,290
The clock strikes twelve.

226
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:55,790
The prompt vanishes.

227
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:57,970
Tomorrow will be messy.

228
00:06:58,430 --> 00:06:59,650
You might say the wrong thing.

229
00:06:59,650 --> 00:07:01,250
You might spill your coffee.

230
00:07:01,650 --> 00:07:02,630
You might get your heart broken.

231
00:07:03,310 --> 00:07:05,190
And for the first time in seven days,

232
00:07:05,570 --> 00:07:06,170
you smile.

233
00:07:06,170 --> 00:07:07,510
Because it's real.

234
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:10,450
If you had one real-life save point

235
00:07:10,450 --> 00:07:12,550
that you could return to anytime,

236
00:07:12,550 --> 00:07:13,630
would you use it to fix a

237
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:15,210
specific moment from your past,

238
00:07:15,650 --> 00:07:17,610
or would you be too afraid of what you might erase?

239
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:19,250
Drop your answer below.
